"<p>Need to upgrade to a larger VPS, move to a different region, or switch hosting providers? Nitrobase can move any deployed app or standalone database between servers (<code>app.move</code> permission) with automatic rollback if anything fails.</p>\n<h2>How Moving an App Works</h2>\n<p>Open <strong>App → Settings → Move to another server</strong>, pick the target ready server (and an off-site storage destination if needed to transfer the backup archive), and start the move job:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Pre-flight &#x26; Backup:</strong> Nitrobase verifies the target server is ready and takes a full consistent backup of the app (database dump + volumes + encrypted <code>.env</code> + pinned commit/version) on the source server.</li>\n<li><strong>Restore on Target:</strong> Restores the app onto the target server with the <strong>same app ID, data, and environment variables</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Health Verification:</strong> Starts the containers on the target server and waits for all health and stability checks to pass.</li>\n<li><strong>Cutover &#x26; Cleanup:</strong> Only after the target instance is confirmed healthy does Nitrobase remove the old copy from the source server.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Failure Safety</h2>\n<p>If any step fails before cutover, Nitrobase deletes the partial copy on the target server and restarts the original app on the source server untouched.</p>\n<h2>Domains &#x26; DNS After Moving</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Free <code>*.sslip.io</code> domains:</strong> Updated automatically to point to the target server's IP address.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom domains:</strong> The move job log lists the exact DNS records (A/CNAME) you need to update at your DNS provider to point to the new server's IP.</li>\n</ul>"